        "content": "<p>Hi, everyone!</p>\n<p>I've been discussing over e-mail with <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span>  the possibility of bringing a small part of <a href=\"https://github.com/d0d1/singer-theorem-lean\">https://github.com/d0d1/singer-theorem-lean</a> to mathlib.</p>\n<p>The initial idea is to start with a short (&lt;300 lines), self-contained PR to AddCombi.</p>\n<p>We could start with the predicate: <code>IsSidon (A : Set G) : Prop</code> over <code>[AddCommMonoid G]</code> saying that equal sums of pairs from <code>A</code> agree up to swapping the two summands.</p>\n<p>Possible first signatures:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSidon.mono</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSidon</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hAB</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsSidon</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isSidon_empty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSidon</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">∅</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">isSidon_singleton</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSidon</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>If you have any thoughts on whether this is a reasonable first PR, please let me know.</p>",
        "id": 594873478,
        "sender_full_name": "David B.",
        "timestamp": 1778682847
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think this would make complete sense as a PR to AddCombi, which I'm happy to review. It could also be a PR to mathlib, but from a quick skim of the linked repo, I think it'd need quite heavy rewriting in review, and it might be easier to do this in a downstream repo first, before trying to get this in mathlib</p>",
        "id": 594893382,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1778687549
    },
